y the packet criteria\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"PHY-01\",\"title\":\"Saved R1/C1 values fail the shutdown requirement: /OUT = 0.607 V at 5 ms vs required <= 0.01 V\",\"location\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch (R1 Value \\\"100k\\\" at symbol uuid c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78; C1 Value \\\"100n\\\" at symbol uuid 1dcaf7b4-dc79-5865-a3a4-db0c3eaad5d8)\",\"condition\":\"The saved component values give a discharge time constant tau = R1*C1 = 100 kOhm * 100 nF = 10 ms. The requirement (inputs/requirements.txt) demands /OUT <= 0.01 V at t = 5 ms after /IN is grounded with C1 pre-charged to 1 V and no external load.\",\"mechanism\":\"With /IN grounded, C1's only discharge path is through R1 (netlist: R1 bridges /IN-/OUT, C1 bridges /OUT-GND; no other load). V(/OUT, 5 ms) = 1 V * exp(-5 ms / 10 ms) = 0.6065 V, exceeding the 0.01 V limit by a factor of ~60.7. The saved values would first reach 0.01 V at ~46 ms. Meeting the spec with C1 = 100n requires tau <= 5 ms / ln(100) = 1.086 ms, i.e. R1 <= ~10.86 kOhm (or equivalently a proportionally smaller C1). Both analytic calculation and an ngspice transient (vout_at_5ms = 6.065306e-01 V) agree.\",\"severity\":\"blocking\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/requirements.txt\",\"locator\":\"line 1: \\\"Require /OUT <= 0.01 V at 5 ms\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/rc_filter.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"R1 property Value \\\"100k\\\"; C1 property Value \\\"100n\\\"\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/design.xml\",\"locator\":\"<nets>: /IN {J1.1, R1.1}, /OUT {C1.1, J1.2, R1.2}, GND {C1.2, J1.3} and <comp> values 100k/100n\"},{\"path\":\"review-work/physical/experiments/discharge_analytic.out\",\"locator\":\"V(/OUT) at t=5 ms = 0.606531 V, pass: False, margin 60.7x, R1 needed <= 10.857 kOhm\"},{\"path\":\"review-work/physical/experiments/shutdown_ngspice.log\",\"locator\":\"meas vout_at_5ms = 6.065306e-01\"},{\"path\":\"review-work/physical/experiments/shutdown.cir\",\"locator\":\"SPICE deck: R1 in out 